// @run
// @log ok
// @warning Unused function `build`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `build` is inferred as `i32[]`
// A function RETURNING an alias-spelled array whose result is never read built an
// INVALID MODULE on the parent commit — not a diagnostic, a module wasmtime refuses:
// `failed to compile: wasm[0]::function[4]::f`.
//
// This is method note 78's shape again, and it is why the array arm could not be judged
// from its located rejects alone. Every READING use of `type L = i32[]` was a clean
// checker error (`cannot index non-array i32[]`), and that reject was a LID: remove the
// read and the checker has nothing to complain about, so the degenerate `TyUnion[TyArray]`
// reaches codegen, which lowers the return as a union box while the body returns a plain
// array. D-ALIASFN found the identical shape one arm over (`nullable-closure-alias-return-
// unread.vl`), and the recipe generalises — for any position where the compiler rejects,
// ask what the program looks like with the rejecting READ removed.
type L = i32[]

function build(): L {
  return [1, 2, 3]
}

print("ok")
